I don't recall that the VS4000 series had the same system disk
limitation as the early MicroVAX 3100 10/10e/20/20e VS3100-30/38/40/48
series.  Those systems had the 1.0xGB boot drive limitation.  I
suppose there may be an upper limit on the boot disk for a VS4000 but
if so its definitely larger than the 1GB safe limit of the older
systems.

A VLC is limited to 5400rpm internal disks though, for power and heat
reasons.



